      "summary": [
        "IMAP advanced settings now store custom OAuth fields and copy them to the default associated SMTP server when the dialog is accepted. An internal issuer UUID is generated and persisted when needed, shared with SMTP, and included in the OAuth object’s cache identity. The selected code replaces the proposed user-entered internal issuer with that generated ID; the separate external issuer identifier and POP3 support visible in accepted source are later changes. The browser test checks saved settings, field enabled states and UUID shape/equality, while the cache unit-test change adds only documentation. No authentication, endpoint validation or runtime test was run."
